00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:49.000
And most of them are things that we are not concerned with.

00:05:49.000 --> 00:05:52.000
You can see there's a bunch of template things here you can use for .NET.

00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:56.000
You can see there's all sorts of things here, MSC, which is like an antiquated library.

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:58.000
And you don't care about any of these things.

00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:02.000
The only thing you want to do is build a Win32 application.

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:03.000
And there's two options here.

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:06.000
One is for a Win32 console application.

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:08.000
One is for a Win32 project.

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:10.000
And the difference between these two

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:12.000
is actually extremely rudimentary.

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:15.000
All it is is, for some reason, way back when they actually

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:19.000
did the original version of Windows,

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:25.000
they decided to segregate how you built basically applications that

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:27.000
could run from a command line, which is something

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:29.000
we'll look at in the future, and ones that are actually

00:06:29.000 --> 00:06:32.000
more like apps like they have a window and stuff like this.

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:36.000
And because they did that, you have to build an app

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:37.000
as one or the other.

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:41.000
And this is actually something that's basically impossible to get around.

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:45.000
There are workarounds for it if you really care, but basically there is no way on Windows,

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:50.000
unlike say on Linux or Mac OS, there is no way to actually build something

00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:57.000
that both works from a command line and works in the standard application mode.

00:06:57.000 --> 00:07:00.000
But we don't have to care about that too much because we're going to be

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:03.000
building a game and games don't really have to do anything from the command

00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:07.000
line in sort of that sort of way.

